Z||000000||moonie||08-15-2001||06:50 PM||||i know some of you will laugh but its a serious questiion.<BR>due to unfortunate circumstances i am moving friday to Kentucky. 150 miles away.<BR>i called the police & they said its against the law for me to obstruct the view from my rearview mirror. i need to tie my army size canvas duffel bag on the luggage rack on the back.<BR>heres the question.<BR>do you think the luggage rack would hold if i hung the duffel bag ( full of clothes ) from it & let it rest on the panel between the tailights. ????<BR>kinda like tying it to a bumper , except in this case it would be the luggage rack.<BR>i know it would look funny as heck , but to save a 6 hour round trip to come back for it , i would look like a geek for 3 hours to <BR>make it in 1 trip.<P>thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||IwannaIRM||08-15-2001||06:56 PM||||I travelled with two duffles strapped to the back of my 84SE.<P>I put them on the right and left of the deck lid so I could still see out of the rearview mirror.  Tied them down real good and drove for two hours.<P>Didn't get hassled by a single trooper.  This was in Utah about 12 years ago so I don't know if this is legal or not now.<P><P>------------------<BR>AIM - SWags2933<P>84 Fiero SE (being modified)<BR>88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||08-15-2001||07:03 PM||||Maybe you shouldn't take this advice, but I say do it anyway.  I really doubt that they would notice, or do anything about it if they did notice.  If you are confident enough to rely on your side mirrors, do what you gotta do.  In both my Fieros and my minivan, I frequently have my rearview blocked.  No big deal.  Unless it's near the end of the month when they need to get their quotas... then be very afraid.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||85Josh||08-15-2001||07:05 PM||||You're moving to Kentucky and a state trooper told you this? Was he from Kentucky? The only mirror that this state requires is the driverside outside mirror. Otherwise all those semi's and box trucks would be in violation. I think I would worry more about my decklid than KY's finest. By the way, welcome to Kentucky!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||08-15-2001||07:08 PM||||That's a crock of . <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> .. You have exterior mirrors that are functional right?  How many delivery trucks would that officer ticket for not having an interior mirror that was usefull? Or simply how many plain ol' pick-ups would get ticketed for having their load block their interior mirror.  I don't think the officer you talked to knew that Fiero's have mirrors on <B>both</B> sides of the car.  I'd get a second opinion on what is legal or not where you live. Anyway that's my thoughts about it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
